Proclamations are issued by the city council to recognize outstanding local events, programs, and nonprofit organizations that are directly associated with the City of Fayetteville. Individuals, for-profit businesses, and organizations and events outside of the City of Fayetteville are not eligible for proclamations.
(1) Proclamation requests must:
a. Be submitted by City of Fayetteville residents or business located in the City;
b. Have the sponsorship of a city council representative;
c. Not duplicate other similar requests; and
d. Not take sides in matters of political controversy, ideological or religious beliefs, or individual conviction.
(2) Proclamations are ceremonial documents signed by the members of the city council and shall only be issued for matters directly associated with the public purpose and benefit of City of Fayetteville, and shall be for the following purposes:
a. Public awareness campaigns;
b. Nonprofit organizations;
c. Arts and cultural celebrations within the City of Fayetteville;
d. Special honors.
(3) The city council reserves the right to modify or deny any proclamation request and shall not grant a proclamation request for any matter that is not associated with the public purpose of the city.
(4) A congratulatory letter is an alternative where proclamation criteria are not met.
(5) Proclamation requests must be submitted to the city clerk in writing for consideration.
(Ord. No. 25-O-35, § 1, 11-20-25)

